# One Makevars for every platform: no Makevars.win, no configure, no C++.
#
# zufuzz's native layer is plain C against R's API only.  Platform
# differences are handled by preprocessor guards in zufuzz.h (see
# ZUFUZZ_HAVE_SHM), not by per-platform build files, so that Windows builds
# the same sources as everywhere else and simply reports that it cannot
# attach to a fuzzing supervisor.
#
# Anything needing C++, a vendored engine, or sanitizer flags belongs in the
# zufuzz.libfuzzer companion package.  If a change here starts to look like
# it needs CXX_STD, that is the signal it is in the wrong repository.

